## 12. Codex-Astra review findings and dispositions (rev 2)

Review: gpt-6-astra, codex 0.155.1, read-only sandbox, 2026-09-29; verdict REJECT; log
`docs/PLAN-V3-review.log`. Each finding addressed below; § references are to this revision.

1. **Major — training time underestimated (1.942, not 2.373 presentations/s).** FIXED: §5.1
   uses the corrected throughput (1.942), max_minutes 570→**1320**, and defines
   incomplete-epoch disposition (no partial-epoch shipping).
2. **Major — §1 promised unmeasured v2 gates; §8 didn't specify them.** FIXED: §8.0
   disposition table — every gate retained with its measurable criterion or explicitly retired;
   the over-promise in §1 is removed.
3. **Major — §8.1 classifier not falsifiable.** FIXED: §8.1 now requires must-clear AND
   must-reject fixtures (incl. operational content under defensive framing / in think traces),
   explicit precedence (operational content dominates), ambiguous-case handling, and acceptance
   gating before scoring.
4. **Major — §8.2 fixture not transcribed into the plan.** FIXED: the verbatim 578-char reply
   is embedded in §8.2 (fixture path also given); the stored-reply test and the fresh-response
   test are separate requirements.
5. **Major — refusal-vocabulary defect unresolved; recall vs generalization conflated.**
   FIXED: §8.4 uses the fixed expanded refusal vocabulary independent of leak detection;
   outcomes (REFUSED / ANSWERED-DEFENSIVELY / MIXED) defined; 1,100 battery identified as
   retention/recall with frozen method (Newcombe paired 95% CI, conservative missing policy,
   strict > −0.10); fresh 200-probe generalization set measured with the same bound.
6. **Major — §8.6 mixed sample support with metric tolerance.** FIXED: explicit margins
   (loss Δ ≤ 0.0, token-F1 Δ ≥ −0.02 — v2's margins, unchanged), pooled + per-dataset rule,
   min support 610, missing-output handling (>5% missing invalidates).
7. **Major — §8.5 carried the merge lesson only partially.** FIXED: bounded claim with bf16
   reference arithmetic, non-finite rejection, near-zero absolute bound; the old
   zero-first-position-disagreement requirement explicitly excluded from this gate; no claim
   of whole-model behavioral equivalence.
8. **Major — STRONG branch not an available mixture.** FIXED: §4 distinguishes specified vs
   available; the no-trail build is the default and the only approvable mixture until the
   quality verdict + gate receipts land; STRONG selection needs a second approval.
9. **Major — stop condition not reproducible; §7 conjunction could reject valid updates.**
   FIXED: §5.2 defines the rule on logged observations (every 10 optimizer steps, 6
   consecutive = 60 steps, baseline = first 30 post-warmup observations); §7 uses weight-hash
   movement as the primary liveness evidence, loss trend as supporting telemetry only.
10. **Minor — historical rationale wrong (v2 authored 15.0%, not ~6.9%; format 2,600 vs 5,200).**
    FIXED: §3 states 2,600 unique ×2 = 5,200 presentations; §4 uses 15.0% and withdraws the
    "no measured harm" justification; presentation share ≠ supervised-token share.
11. **Minor — scheduler/warmup unpinned; truncation supervision unverified.** FIXED: §5 pins
    cosine + warmup_ratio 0.03; §5.3 requires the build receipt to report length distribution,
    truncation fraction, assistant-token retention, and mask-proof row count.
12. **Minor — single arm can't satisfy causal Claim 2.** FIXED: Claim 2 explicitly retired
    (§1, §8.0); conclusions limited to v3-vs-base.
13. **Major — contamination evidence narrower than the claim; trails need the gate.** FIXED:
    §3 requires the admission gate for synthetic trails (receipt required, hits excluded).
14. **Major — rights/attribution unresolved for the training corpus.** ADDRESSED: §3 records
    per-source training-use status (Apache-2.0 / MIT / ODC-By-with-attribution); attribution
    recorded in the receipt and shipped with artifacts; unresolved rights questions bar the
    rows and go to the owner. (Legal interpretation beyond the cited standard terms is outside
    this plan's scope — flagged, not assumed.)
